Reimplement the desktop app with Tauri 2, reusing the web app's Elm code

Purpose:
A local-file desktop Gingko Writer (.gkw/.gko/.md, no server) built on
Tauri 2 instead of Electron, sharing the Elm document editor with the
web app so desktop and web don't drift apart.

Approach:
- Rust backend in client/src-tauri/: doc/home window lifecycle, native
  menus with recent documents, file I/O with swap files and temp
  backups, per-document undo history as JSON stores under app data,
  recent documents + per-file settings store, txt/json export, docx
  export via pandoc, JSON import via the Elm worker, file associations,
  single-instance file-open, save-changes dialogs (all native dialogs
  through tauri-plugin-dialog, attached to their window).
- All commands are #[tauri::command(async)] and window creation from
  main-thread contexts (menu events, single-instance callback, macOS
  Reopen/Opened) runs on a worker thread. Tauri 2 runs sync commands on
  the main thread, and creating a WebviewWindow there deadlocks the
  event loop on Windows (wry#583): the window stays at about:blank.
- Opening a file that is already open focuses its window and reports
  success. Paths are compared canonically (casing/prefixes differ
  between the recent list, the command line and dialogs). Opens are
  serialized, so a double-click can't open the same file twice.
- Menu actions reach only the focused document: Rust uses emit_to(label)
  and the renderer listens on its own window. A plain emit(), or a
  global listen(), reaches every window.
- Every window has its own menu, built with the window and updated in
  place: Save/Saved follows the document, and the Edit menu swaps between
  text and card commands while a card's textarea has focus. A single
  menu shared by all windows doesn't work on Windows (it is destroyed
  along with the first window that closes), and replacing a menu bar
  (set_menu) makes the window visibly re-layout. Updates run on the main
  thread, like window events. On macOS the menu bar is app-wide, so the
  focused window's menu is installed on focus.
- Saving never silently loses content:
  - Untitled documents live in the temp dir; the file is created up
    front, so Save As works on an untouched document. Save As copies the
    file, then has Elm write the current content (SaveRequested, which
    folds in the card being edited) and waits for that write. The temp
    file is removed afterwards.
  - Save As onto the document's own path returns early (copying a file
    onto itself and then cleaning up would delete its undo history).
  - Closing a document with unsaved changes waits for the confirmed
    write; a close whose save fails stays open.
  - Failed saves reach Elm as SaveError; the save indicator shows a red
    "Save failed" badge (error as tooltip) until the next good save.
  - Exit closes each window, so every document runs its close handling
    (the save prompt for untitled docs) instead of the app quitting.
- Security: the app commands are declared in an app manifest (build.rs,
  permissions/autogenerated/) so they are subject to capabilities. Only
  the home and doc windows get them; the support modal only gets window
  close, because the FAQ modal loads a third-party script.
- Frontend glue in client/src/tauri/ ports src/electron/renderer.js and
  home.js to Tauri invoke/events, including the commit-tree port
  (hashing with hash-wasm, like the web app's data.js). client/esbuild-tauri.mjs builds Elm + JS + tailwind
  + static assets into client/tauri-web/; release builds (tauri build)
  use --production (elm make --optimize, minified).
- Elm: Electron.elm is ported to the opaque Page.Doc API
  (opaqueUpdate/opaqueIncoming, Doc.History, data owned by the wrapper).
  New documents seed card "1" themselves, since the shared defaultTree
  is empty (the web app creates the first card via its database flow).
- bundle.icon lists PNGs (256px first) besides .ico/.icns: on Linux
  generate_context!() takes the first .png as the window icon and
  panics without one.

Constraints:
- The web app must behave exactly as upstream. Shared modules only gain
  desktop-only pieces: SavedToFile/ClickedExport/DataSaved in
  Page.Doc.Incoming (plus SaveRequested/SaveError), viewFullscreenButtonsDesktop in Doc.Fullscreen, an
  exposed UI.Header.viewExportMenu, the ShortcutsModal viewShortcuts
  arity fix.
- The Electron app (client/app, src/electron) is left in place, untouched.
- Don't grant app commands to any window that loads remote content.

Rebase notes (monorepo layout, upstream since 2026-09):
- All files live under client/. The Tauri usage docs are a section at
  the end of the root README.md, because upstream merged client/README.md
  into it.
- client/bun.lockb: take upstream's version, then regenerate it with
  `bun install --lockfile-only` in client/ so it includes @tauri-apps/api
  and @tauri-apps/cli again.
- client/src-tauri/gen/schemas/ is regenerated by every build and is
  gitignored (as in Tauri's app template); client/src-tauri/.gitattributes
  pins LF so the generated permissions/*.toml files don't show as modified
  after a build on core.autocrlf checkouts.

